  "summary": "Major funding rounds underscore continued investment in health-tech verticals, with Angle Health reaching a $2.7 billion valuation on $600 million in equity financing, Ayble Health securing $16 million for virtual digestive health services, and Inspiren raising $70 million for an AI senior care platform. On the regulatory and policy front, the Trump administration is promoting a GENEROUS program to offer cheaper drugs through state Medicaid programs, while CMS is expanding its outcomes-based ACCESS model starting spring 2027 to cover heart failure, COPD, substance use disorders, and tobacco cessation. In clinical breakthroughs, Ultragenyx's Fayuvi became the first FDA-approved gene therapy for Sanfilippo syndrome type A, while Roche and Genentech opened a new Boston R&D center to expand research capabilities. Healthcare infrastructure continues evolving with efforts to advance interstate telehealth licensure and physical AI deployments addressing hospital logistics fragmentation, though emerging concerns about AI governance—including rogue agents and careful scrutiny for older adult populations—highlight the need for thoughtful implementation alongside innovation.",
